heres the deal though, I suspect write buffer is coherent meaning before enqueuing
the full cost of coherence is paid.

why is it useful then, as explained in amd manuals it serves two purposes:

<a> reads have higher priority than writes so its possible a write enqueue might 
not complete because of arbitration on the dcache.  placing it in the write buffer
allows load store unit to not block.

<b> dcache line allocation can take time if eviction is involved. again you want to 
avoid backpressuring lsu

